 * Support customize action(reboot or invoke dispatch script) if daemon
   stoped/crashed
 * Allow daemon to send out securty events via gRPC for performance and securty
   concern.
 * Set the eBPF priority of monitor function to worse priorty to make sure
   we don't track events been expcitly allowed/dropped.
 * TCP SYNC flood protection -- tried, it seems aya compiled code cannot pass
   kernel validation. Need deep investigation.
 * UDP flood protection:
    * For well known protocol (e.g. DNS), eBPF drop invalid packet
    * For user's specific protocol, allow user to define check rule like as
      array of `<offset>: <expected_value>`
